(text "OPERATOR INPUTS (RC-filtered ADC)" (at 20.32 139.7 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid bb9d41ba-a051-4413-8d82-60cb983a13be))
(text "NOTES. A concept drawn by Claude at Bob Drzyzgula's direction, October 2026: not built, not tested, values not checked." (at 20.32 259.3 0) (effects (font (size 1.15 1.15) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 4198e21c-6a15-4321-95f0-2bfb6eeb4149))
(text "1. After Freescale AN1662: zero-cross interrupt sets a timer alarm (or a PIO program); at the firing delay a ~100 us gate pulse fires the" (at 20.32 261.8 0) (effects (font (size 1.15 1.15)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 856b131f-d410-45eb-a586-5c9de8e0f8e8))
(text "   triac; hand-wheel period from edge timestamps; speed loop every half-cycle (120 Hz); stall watchdog. Added: isolation, relay, inputs." (at 20.32 264.3 0) (effects (font (size 1.15 1.15)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid dd56d6d0-67cb-4b12-83d5-888de60f9786))
(text "2. Pins (RP2350B): FIRE GP4; RELAY GP5; ZC GP6; HALL (index) GP7; ENC_A/B GP2/GP3 (PIO counter); STITCH GP10; HEEL GP11; NEEDLE GP12;" (at 20.32 266.8 0) (effects (font (size 1.15 1.15)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid ca4904bf-44d2-4eaf-afde-5655d49df00c))
(text "   knee, pedal, FSR, limit on ADC0-3 (GP40-43); ADC4-7 spare; GP8/GP9 UART1 for debug (or USB serial). Avoid GP0, GP23, GP25 (PSRAM, key, LED)." (at 20.32 269.3 0) (effects (font (size 1.15 1.15)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 1c24c2a6-8918-4609-8112-d639c7636b71))
(text "3. PS1 feeds VSYS through D2, so USB may stay plugged in (the control side is SELV). Flash by UF2 (BOOTSEL) or SWD. Drive GP4 at 8-12 mA." (at 20.32 271.8 0) (effects (font (size 1.15 1.15)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 525f7cbf-455f-4cfa-ab6d-a039f6ad570f))
(text "4. Fire only after a zero-cross has been seen and the command is zero; close K1 last and open it first. Never scope the line side." (at 20.32 274.3 0) (effects (font (size 1.15 1.15)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid e6e1191b-7546-4441-8f24-3609a33a78be))
(text "5. R7/R8: ~3.9 mA peak in the H11AA1; R11: ~8 mA into U3 from 3.3 V; R6/C2 fitted only if a snubberless triac false-fires." (at 20.32 276.8 0) (effects (font (size 1.15 1.15)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 849cfb5e-6db2-4368-abc3-03d50af4d1a4))
(text "6. On a WeAct RP2350B Core board, feed PS1 to the 5V pin: the board has its own diode from USB VBUS, so D2 may be left out." (at 20.32 279.3 0) (effects (font (size 1.15 1.15)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid fe8c0c9d-5742-46d2-b8d1-c1a4b42e2b6c))
(text "7. Heel: momentary switch to GND in either pedal (J5 pin 4, J6 pin 3); a heel tap sends the needle to its other stop." (at 20.32 281.8 0) (effects (font (size 1.15 1.15)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 27b2bec2-3571-4878-9a28-cb7cdcbf54fd))
(text "8. Encoder U5/U6 (ring of alternating magnets) optional: stops taught and landed by angle; 5-wire cable (3V3, GND, index, A, B)." (at 20.32 284.3 0) (effects (font (size 1.15 1.15)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 5e3a2dbf-9d51-45b3-b16c-6aa37ced7a0d))
